WEBVTT

00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:15.473
[girl] All right. Next agenda item.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:19.227
We've been having recurring problems
with one of the students.

00:00:19.811 --> 00:00:22.063
She just came in to the school this year.

00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:23.481
Midari Ikishima.

00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:24.941
Over the last month,

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:28.278
people have begun calling her
the "Destroyer of Dens"

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.988
She's well-earned this nickname

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:33.074
by gambling
at several locations across campus,

00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:35.535
and has ousted leaders at seven of them.

00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:39.247
Five of them were previously
under Student Council jurisdiction.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:43.334
None of the usage fees
for the dens have been paid.

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:46.129
And she's made no indication
that she intends to pay.

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:50.508
Sayaka, I'll leave this to you.

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:52.177
I've made the arrangements.

00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:54.763
-Miharutaki.
-Hmm.

00:00:54.846 --> 00:00:57.766
Understood. I'll get it done today.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:03.271
Sachiko, you're in a good mood today.

00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:04.856
That's because I am.

00:01:07.108 --> 00:01:09.861
[Sachiko] We have a wealth
of interesting first-years.

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:14.908
-[Tsuzura] Good morning, Mary!
-[Mary grunting]

00:01:15.784 --> 00:01:17.994
Oh. Hey, Tsuzura. Good morning.

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:24.793
I can't believe we start today.
We have a gambling den.

00:01:24.876 --> 00:01:28.171
I was so excited
I don't think I slept at all last night.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.799
Are you sure
you're really a high-schooler?

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:32.926
Everyone here acts so freaking weird.

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:34.177
Huh?

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.054
What? You okay?

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.101
[Mary gasping] Are those razors?

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:42.268
Who put those there?

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:43.728
There's nothing I can do.

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:47.440
You know, I'm a Mitten.

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:50.860
[Tsuzura] But it'll be okay.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.613
Each step will bring me closer
to being a winner.

00:01:53.696 --> 00:01:56.074
I can handle anything if it's temporary.

00:01:56.157 --> 00:01:57.742
I'm not gonna lose now.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.998
TWIN

00:02:45.081 --> 00:02:46.541
LIBRARY PREP ROOM NUMBER TWO

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.879
-Huh?
-Oh!

00:02:50.962 --> 00:02:52.505
Good morning, you two!

00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:54.507
Welcome! I cleaned up!

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:59.637
Yukimi Togakushi!
What do you think you're doing in my den?

00:02:59.721 --> 00:03:03.516
Simple. I'm the club president
and I still have the key.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.353
I didn't ask how you got in!
What? Are you trying to take the den back?

00:03:07.437 --> 00:03:08.271
I swear I'm not!

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:09.731
Nothing like that.

00:03:09.814 --> 00:03:12.901
I just want to keep using this room
for my club. That's all.

00:03:12.984 --> 00:03:14.652
None of the members show up here,

00:03:14.736 --> 00:03:16.779
so the club won't interfere with gambling.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:19.365
Can I, please? I'll even hide.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.994
Oh. Come on, Mary. I think it'll be good.

00:03:23.077 --> 00:03:23.912
Huh?

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:28.291
Until yesterday, Togakushi was the one
running the gambling den.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.793
Don't you think she might have
some good suggestions for us?

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:32.837
Yeah. Nobody cared about it.

00:03:32.921 --> 00:03:34.964
Why would I wanna listen to her ideas?

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:37.675
-[Tsuzura] I guess.
-[both] Hmm?

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.261
She did just lose all her space.

00:03:40.803 --> 00:03:42.847
I think that must be pretty hard.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.684
Forget about her.
You should put yourself first.

00:03:46.768 --> 00:03:47.810
Did you forget that you…

00:03:50.271 --> 00:03:51.522
[Mary groaning]

00:03:55.652 --> 00:03:57.153
[Mary groaning]

00:04:00.657 --> 00:04:01.950
All right. You're in.

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:04.077
You'd better be prepared to work.

00:04:04.702 --> 00:04:07.163
The most challenging thing
about running a gambling den

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.082
would definitely be the money.

00:04:09.165 --> 00:04:11.000
I picked Library Prep Room Number Two

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:13.002
because it was one
of the cheapest options,

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:16.589
but the fee I owe the Student Council
is still half-a-million yen a month.

00:04:16.673 --> 00:04:17.840
Pretty pricey.

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:20.593
And the fee for two people
is even higher than that.

00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:23.638
You would need to donate
at least 700,000 yen a month.

00:04:23.721 --> 00:04:25.473
Then you gotta include
the amount necessary

00:04:25.556 --> 00:04:27.850
to change up Hanatemari's status.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.102
Oh. About that.

00:04:29.185 --> 00:04:32.146
I heard there's an easier way
to reverse a house pet's status.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.357
Easier than waiting for a donation day.

00:04:34.899 --> 00:04:36.943
Isn't there an exception
with Student Council

00:04:37.026 --> 00:04:38.987
if you donate a million yen?

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.655
If I'm being honest,

00:04:40.738 --> 00:04:43.741
I didn't really think aiming for that
would be realistic, but

00:04:45.076 --> 00:04:47.245
I don't feel like that anymore.

00:04:47.328 --> 00:04:50.957
So if we take all of that into account,
it's 1,7 mil.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:53.751
I need to make this amount
in the fastest way possible.

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:55.962
You really think we can do that?

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.006
Of course, we can!

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:04.804
[Tsuzura] <i>Mary can do it.</i>
<i>I know my prince can do anything.</i>

00:05:05.346 --> 00:05:06.180
Hmm?

00:05:06.723 --> 00:05:08.141
One question.

00:05:08.224 --> 00:05:09.892
Do we know what game we'll play?

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:12.395
Of course. I've already figured that out.

00:05:16.733 --> 00:05:18.276
[Mary] We'll use this.

00:05:27.368 --> 00:05:28.411
LIBRARY PREP ROOM NO. 1

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.418
Pardon me, ladies.

00:05:36.961 --> 00:05:39.422
What's up, you bitch?

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:40.923
You know why I'm here.

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:44.177
Sakura Miharutaki, Beautification Council.

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:45.678
Huh?

00:05:45.762 --> 00:05:49.057
Don't play dumb, "Den Destroyer" Ikishima.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:51.934
What? You got a problem
with me gambling on campus?

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:54.479
That is not what I have an issue with.

00:05:54.562 --> 00:05:57.940
You've taken over seven dens,
you're the one with the usage rights.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:02.195
But that ownership transfer saddled you
with the usage fees for those dens.

00:06:02.278 --> 00:06:03.154
COLLECTION LETTER

00:06:03.237 --> 00:06:05.114
The Student Council
is renting you those dens,

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:06.532
and we're here to collect.

00:06:06.616 --> 00:06:08.201
You owe us five million yen.

00:06:09.285 --> 00:06:13.414
Payment is due today,
and we expect the amount in full.

00:06:14.248 --> 00:06:15.625
Five million yen?

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.711
Five million yen. Wow.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.966
That's hilarious! [laughing]

00:06:25.301 --> 00:06:27.095
Hey! What's so funny?

00:06:27.178 --> 00:06:30.765
Are you stupid?
No one in this room has that kinda money.

00:06:30.848 --> 00:06:32.975
We took our money
and shoved it up Mickey's ass.

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.394
That's enough!

00:06:34.477 --> 00:06:36.729
If we have to,
we can take the money by force!

00:06:36.813 --> 00:06:39.732
Threaten us as much as you want.
It won't come back.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:41.776
Search them.

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.863
You can't touch my stuff! [gasping]

00:06:45.947 --> 00:06:48.449
We are busy with administrative duties.

00:06:48.533 --> 00:06:50.159
I suggest you comply.

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.077
And I'll remind you,

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.372
the Beautification Council
has the authority to arrest students.

00:06:54.455 --> 00:06:56.416
Uh, you can't do that to me.

00:06:56.499 --> 00:06:58.626
Chill out for a second

00:06:58.709 --> 00:07:00.711
Isn't anyone else bored to tears

00:07:00.795 --> 00:07:03.631
by arguing about stupid crap like this?

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:06.884
Why don't we gamble instead?

00:07:06.968 --> 00:07:08.094
Go on.

00:07:08.177 --> 00:07:12.098
Well, it sounds like we both want to solve
this problem as quickly as possible.

00:07:12.181 --> 00:07:13.349
Am I right?

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:16.227
Lucky for us,
this place has so many games.

00:07:16.811 --> 00:07:18.980
I'll even let you pick which one.

00:07:19.063 --> 00:07:21.983
Take a load off
and play a round of your favorite.

00:07:22.066 --> 00:07:24.527
If you win, I'll pay right away.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.446
But if you lose, you get out.

00:07:26.529 --> 00:07:27.488
Whatcha think

00:07:27.572 --> 00:07:31.159
If you have the money to gamble,
that means you can pay us this instant.

00:07:33.703 --> 00:07:34.620
I accept.

00:07:35.204 --> 00:07:37.123
Okay. It's decided.

00:07:37.707 --> 00:07:39.167
What are we playing?

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:50.136
[Midari] Hmm?

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:58.769
I want a dice game.

00:08:00.229 --> 00:08:02.315
This will be Make It Or Break It.

00:08:02.398 --> 00:08:05.151
Guess if the upcoming dice roll
will be even or odd.

00:08:05.234 --> 00:08:07.069
Will that be simple enough for you?

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:10.781
Yeah. Now hurry up and throw.

00:08:10.865 --> 00:08:12.116
No.

00:08:12.617 --> 00:08:14.202
You throw the dice.

00:08:14.285 --> 00:08:16.287
I'll be the one to make the guess

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:17.788
Huh?

00:08:17.872 --> 00:08:20.708
Ma'am, are you sure that's a good idea?

00:08:20.791 --> 00:08:24.003
If she's the one with the dice,
who knows what tricks she'll try to pull.

00:08:24.086 --> 00:08:25.796
My word is final.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.883
Toss the dice, Midari Ikishima.

00:08:33.221 --> 00:08:37.099
Oh, good! I don't know
what you've got up your sleeve,

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.809
but I wanna see!

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:41.687
Even or odd?

00:08:41.771 --> 00:08:42.688
It's even.

00:08:42.772 --> 00:08:45.316
Oh, wow. She didn't even hesitate.

00:08:45.399 --> 00:08:47.443
You carry yourself confidently.

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:50.071
You're a woman that knows what she wants.

00:08:50.154 --> 00:08:53.074
Let's get this over with.
I want to see what you rolled.

00:08:53.157 --> 00:08:55.826
Oh fine. You're no fun.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:59.080
All right. Time for the big reveal.

00:08:59.163 --> 00:09:00.831
Here it is!

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:03.209
Six. It's even!

00:09:03.292 --> 00:09:05.294
The Council Chief wins!

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:09.257
Oh wow. Looks like she got it right.

00:09:09.799 --> 00:09:11.467
-Hey.
-Fine.

00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:13.219
There's five million.

00:09:14.804 --> 00:09:17.056
What compelled you to choose even?

00:09:17.139 --> 00:09:18.724
Did you go with a feeling?

00:09:18.808 --> 00:09:21.727
You already know the answer,
so why ask me?

00:09:21.811 --> 00:09:25.231
-Make sure it's all there.
-Uh, well, we were kinda wondering too.

00:09:26.566 --> 00:09:28.818
Simple. I saw through their trick.

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:30.903
Then I turned it back around on them.

00:09:32.488 --> 00:09:33.948
They tricked us?

00:09:34.031 --> 00:09:36.242
Yes. Ikishima likely predicted

00:09:36.325 --> 00:09:38.786
that we would play a dice game
from the beginning.

00:09:38.869 --> 00:09:42.540
But how could she have possibly known
which game you would choose to play?

00:09:42.623 --> 00:09:44.500
It was a matter of logic.

00:09:44.584 --> 00:09:47.295
The room was staged
for me to pick that game.

00:09:47.378 --> 00:09:49.005
Take a look around us.

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:51.674
There's shogi, go, chess, checkers,

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:55.469
mahjong, backgammon,
and a collection of video games

00:09:55.553 --> 00:09:57.555
All those options take time.

00:09:57.638 --> 00:09:59.098
I said I was in a hurry,

00:09:59.181 --> 00:10:01.559
so of course
I'd pick whichever was the fastest.

00:10:03.144 --> 00:10:04.854
[Sakura] That left me with two options.

00:10:04.937 --> 00:10:06.355
Cards or dice.

00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:09.567
Unfortunately, these are
exceptionally easy to cheat with.

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:11.360
But there's no helping that,

00:10:11.444 --> 00:10:13.571
so I was forced to choose between the two.

00:10:13.654 --> 00:10:15.323
Oh. I see no.

00:10:15.406 --> 00:10:18.576
Huh.
So what made you choose the dice then?

00:10:18.659 --> 00:10:21.579
I'll not pick a game
that I know I can't win.

00:10:22.246 --> 00:10:24.081
<i>When I picked up the die earlier,</i>

00:10:24.165 --> 00:10:26.834
<i>I couldn't help but notice</i>
<i>that the "two" side was a little heavier.</i>

00:10:26.917 --> 00:10:31.088
That's why I wanted you to toss the dice,
and I would be the one to guess the roll.

00:10:32.673 --> 00:10:35.426
She didn't need to throw the dice
to figure it out.

00:10:35.509 --> 00:10:37.386
I'm still confused about all this.

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:39.805
If the "two" side was down,
it would've shown a "five."

00:10:39.889 --> 00:10:41.724
But when she rolled,
it turned over as a "six."

00:10:41.807 --> 00:10:45.269
Ikishima wanted to make it obvious to me
that she had added weight to the die.

00:10:46.354 --> 00:10:49.023
<i>Because then she'd swap out</i>
<i>the loaded one.</i>

00:10:50.608 --> 00:10:51.525
Five.

00:10:51.609 --> 00:10:53.361
Which means the new weighted die
in the game

00:10:53.444 --> 00:10:55.029
would be rigged to throw evens.

00:10:55.112 --> 00:10:56.405
The rest was easy.

00:10:56.489 --> 00:10:58.949
Al that's left is two, four, and six.

00:11:01.285 --> 00:11:02.536
That's it.

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:05.539
Logically,
there was no way for me to lose.

00:11:05.623 --> 00:11:09.293
Oh wow. She came up
with offense and defense right away.

00:11:09.377 --> 00:11:10.544
She's so amazing!

00:11:10.628 --> 00:11:12.588
My business is done here.

00:11:13.297 --> 00:11:14.882
I have other collections.

00:11:16.133 --> 00:11:17.301
Hold up a sec.

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:19.887
Don't be a sore loser.

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:25.393
Look here. I've got 30 million.

00:11:26.602 --> 00:11:28.062
Please go another round.

00:11:28.145 --> 00:11:29.814
Let's play again

00:11:29.897 --> 00:11:31.524
W-why would she play,

00:11:31.607 --> 00:11:34.443
especially when she caught
your weighted dice in the first game?

00:11:34.527 --> 00:11:37.405
Yeah. I thought
you might bring that up again.

00:11:37.488 --> 00:11:41.534
So this time I promise I'll be a good girl
and I won't touch the dice at all.

00:11:41.617 --> 00:11:44.161
And I'll even let you be the one
to make the guess.

00:11:44.245 --> 00:11:45.204
What do you think?

00:11:45.287 --> 00:11:47.123
What are you scheming?

00:11:47.206 --> 00:11:49.208
We know the dice are going to roll even.

00:11:50.334 --> 00:11:52.712
So that means
there's no reason not to play.

00:11:53.295 --> 00:11:56.090
It's like finding free money
out on the street.

00:11:56.173 --> 00:11:59.969
Come on! Hurry up
and play with me, Sakura Miharutaki!

00:12:00.553 --> 00:12:03.723
Don't you want 30 million yen?

00:12:04.306 --> 00:12:05.224
Not really.

00:12:05.307 --> 00:12:06.183
Huh?

00:12:06.684 --> 00:12:09.812
You probably switched out the die again
right after the game,

00:12:09.895 --> 00:12:11.814
just when you thought no one was looking.

00:12:11.897 --> 00:12:14.984
Or you haven't and you just want
to convince everyone you did.

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:17.778
Mind games aren't very interesting
for me to play.

00:12:17.862 --> 00:12:19.238
So, I'm not going to.

00:12:24.326 --> 00:12:25.453
[Midari moaning]

00:12:25.536 --> 00:12:29.373
What was her deal?
She had totally negative vibes.

00:12:29.457 --> 00:12:32.251
She didn't know
what she was talking about.

00:12:32.877 --> 00:12:34.003
<i>Sure.</i>

00:12:34.086 --> 00:12:37.173
<i>Miharutaki did get one thing wrong</i>
<i>about the match.</i>

00:12:37.256 --> 00:12:39.842
<i>I didn't touch the dice</i>
<i>after the game finished.</i>

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:42.136
<i>She's reading into things too much.</i>

00:12:42.636 --> 00:12:47.641
<i>She assumed that I swapped one loaded die</i>
<i>with another, which made her choose even.</i>

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:51.520
<i>But she was wrong.</i>

00:12:52.521 --> 00:12:56.025
<i>The die that I ended up swapping in</i>
<i>was completely legit.</i>

00:12:56.525 --> 00:12:58.778
<i>It just so happened</i>
<i>to roll an even number.</i>

00:12:59.528 --> 00:13:03.741
<i>She'll get nowhere with that talent</i>
<i>if she stays so straight-and-narrow.</i>

00:13:03.824 --> 00:13:06.952
<i>She's gotta learn to be flexible,</i>
<i>or she'll break.</i>

00:13:08.078 --> 00:13:10.164
[Midari] <i>Well,</i>
<i>I can't think of a single person</i>

00:13:10.247 --> 00:13:13.334
<i>who can break the President</i>
<i>of the Beautification Council.</i>

00:13:14.043 --> 00:13:15.461
<i>At least not yet.</i>

00:13:18.547 --> 00:13:20.257
That was incredible, right?

00:13:20.341 --> 00:13:22.009
-Yeah.
-That was a heck of a comeback!

00:13:22.092 --> 00:13:24.595
Huh? So is this a new gambling den?

00:13:24.678 --> 00:13:25.971
You wanna check it out?

00:13:26.555 --> 00:13:28.474
LIMITED GRAND OPENING
LIBRARY PREP ROOM NO. 2

00:13:30.309 --> 00:13:33.979
Welcome, gentlemen!
You found the Literary Club!

00:13:36.065 --> 00:13:36.982
[both grunting]

00:13:40.069 --> 00:13:41.487
All right, good sir.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:44.657
Let me explain the rules of the game,
and then we can play.

00:13:45.157 --> 00:13:46.408
It's all pretty simple.

00:13:46.492 --> 00:13:48.494
We'll be using these three dice today.

00:13:49.078 --> 00:13:51.539
First, we let our customer select
one of these options,

00:13:51.622 --> 00:13:53.499
and then they give it a toss
onto the table.

00:13:53.582 --> 00:13:56.961
The dealer picks a different dice to throw
and compares the results.

00:13:57.044 --> 00:13:59.004
Whoever has the higher number wins.

00:13:59.088 --> 00:14:02.132
Ah.
I guess that seems pretty straightforward.

00:14:02.216 --> 00:14:04.009
But these don't look like regular dice.

00:14:04.093 --> 00:14:07.263
Yes. These are custom made,
so the faces are unique.

00:14:07.346 --> 00:14:10.891
The black dice
has "three," "four," and "eight."

00:14:10.975 --> 00:14:13.894
The white dice
has "one," "five," and "nine."

00:14:13.978 --> 00:14:17.022
The red dice
has "two," "six," and "seven."

00:14:17.106 --> 00:14:20.067
So some of these dice
are weaker than others.

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:22.528
You're sure there's not some sort of trick
to these things?

00:14:22.611 --> 00:14:26.031
Of course not. Feel free
to examine them to your heart's content.

00:14:26.115 --> 00:14:27.241
Hmm.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.286
Cool. Guess I'll try it out.

00:14:30.369 --> 00:14:31.829
And, not to rain on the fun,

00:14:31.912 --> 00:14:34.123
but I'd like to point out
that our den's current policy

00:14:34.206 --> 00:14:36.292
has a gambling limit
of three times per day.

00:14:36.375 --> 00:14:38.127
We're running a special event,

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:40.045
so we want to make sure
everyone who visits

00:14:40.129 --> 00:14:41.797
gets a chance to enjoy themselves.

00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:43.674
Ah. So that's what that means.

00:14:43.757 --> 00:14:45.801
Can my first bet be 10,000 yen?

00:14:45.885 --> 00:14:47.011
That'll be great.

00:14:47.094 --> 00:14:49.805
Now, please choose your dice,
if you wouldn't mind.

00:14:49.889 --> 00:14:51.140
Hmm.

00:14:51.223 --> 00:14:52.808
I'll go with this one.

00:14:53.392 --> 00:14:54.810
Did that one call to you?

00:14:54.894 --> 00:14:58.314
Well, if I wanna win,
I need to roll a nine. Should be easy.

00:14:58.397 --> 00:15:01.817
Wonderful. I'll pick the red dice
for the first round today.

00:15:01.901 --> 00:15:04.862
Okay. Make sure we toss them out
at the same time.

00:15:04.945 --> 00:15:06.071
On the count of three.

00:15:06.155 --> 00:15:07.489
One, two, three.

00:15:07.573 --> 00:15:09.074
<i>A three-round limit?</i>

00:15:09.158 --> 00:15:11.035
We gotta preserve the magic.

00:15:11.118 --> 00:15:13.829
We don't wanna make them do
the same thing every time.

00:15:13.913 --> 00:15:17.583
That's why I plan to change
the game we offer on a weekly basis.

00:15:17.666 --> 00:15:20.628
Isn't that a waste of time
if we're already making a profit?

00:15:20.711 --> 00:15:21.587
Why change it?

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:24.590
Easy. Someone might figure us out.

00:15:27.176 --> 00:15:29.011
-Aw, man.
-You botched it.

00:15:29.094 --> 00:15:30.596
I can't believe this.

00:15:30.679 --> 00:15:31.597
One more time!

00:15:32.181 --> 00:15:34.975
Great. Which die would you like this time?

00:15:35.059 --> 00:15:38.228
Picking red. I think
the dealer chose this one for a reason.

00:15:38.312 --> 00:15:39.229
Hmm.

00:15:39.313 --> 00:15:41.941
I guess I'll go
with the black dice this time around.

00:15:42.024 --> 00:15:44.485
Are you ready? Let's roll!

00:15:47.071 --> 00:15:49.239
Heck yeah! That's how you do it!

00:15:49.323 --> 00:15:51.075
Congratulations on your win!

00:15:51.158 --> 00:15:53.744
I totally knew
there was something up with the red die.

00:15:54.453 --> 00:15:56.747
<i>Everything's playing out</i>
<i>just like Mary said.</i>

00:15:57.331 --> 00:15:59.541
This is a good game
for us to start with.

00:15:59.625 --> 00:16:02.169
It's random, so we'll probably lose a few.

00:16:02.252 --> 00:16:03.879
But they'll come back for more

00:16:03.963 --> 00:16:06.632
because they're also able
to win a few games.

00:16:06.715 --> 00:16:09.635
This is your last round today.
What would you like to do?

00:16:09.718 --> 00:16:13.472
I gotta bet again.
50,000, and I'm gonna stick with red.

00:16:13.555 --> 00:16:16.892
All right. I'll keep things simple
and use the black dice.

00:16:16.976 --> 00:16:18.394
Here we go.

00:16:26.485 --> 00:16:28.153
So how'd we do?

00:16:28.904 --> 00:16:30.489
Day one revenue,

00:16:31.407 --> 00:16:33.534
a total of 300,000 yen!

00:16:33.617 --> 00:16:34.910
We did it!

00:16:34.994 --> 00:16:37.538
With the seed money,
we have one million yen.

00:16:37.621 --> 00:16:40.666
That means 1,7 million
is well within our reach.

00:16:40.749 --> 00:16:43.002
I'm going to make Tsuzura a human again.

00:16:43.085 --> 00:16:45.295
I can get the money for that easily.

00:16:45.379 --> 00:16:46.672
This is amazing!

00:16:46.755 --> 00:16:48.924
I didn't think
we could make this much right away!

00:16:49.008 --> 00:16:52.678
I knew we would bring in some,
but not this much.

00:16:52.761 --> 00:16:54.680
The maid outfit was a nice touch, right?

00:16:54.763 --> 00:16:57.641
Yeah. I thought you were crazy
with that idea, at first,

00:16:57.725 --> 00:16:59.184
but, in the end, it really paid off.

00:16:59.268 --> 00:17:01.937
That might have helped,
but you picked the perfect game to play.

00:17:02.021 --> 00:17:03.397
People were eating it up!

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:05.149
It was such a good idea!

00:17:05.232 --> 00:17:07.943
We were so right. Mary is the best!

00:17:08.652 --> 00:17:11.655
Praise me all you want,
it won't get you anywhere.

00:17:11.739 --> 00:17:14.950
Mary. Mary.

00:17:15.034 --> 00:17:16.660
Mary.

00:17:16.744 --> 00:17:18.454
-Uh, I really don't…
-Mary.

00:17:18.537 --> 00:17:21.707
-Mary! Mary!
-Let's talk about tomorrow.

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:25.586
-Uh…
-Mary! Mary!

00:17:25.669 --> 00:17:28.756
Mary! Mary!

00:17:28.839 --> 00:17:30.424
-Mary!
-Shut up!

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:32.843
Ultra special!

00:17:35.429 --> 00:17:37.056
-No!
-[game announcer] <i>K-O!</i>

00:17:37.139 --> 00:17:39.058
<i>You win!</i>

00:17:39.141 --> 00:17:42.519
Runa, how are you always so good
at video games?

00:17:42.603 --> 00:17:46.023
You just get good
at what you love when you do it a lot.

00:17:46.106 --> 00:17:48.400
Too bad you can't get good at growing.

00:17:48.484 --> 00:17:51.278
Shut up! I just measured
and was, like, two millimeters taller!

00:17:51.361 --> 00:17:53.489
-You two are having fun.
-Huh?

00:17:53.572 --> 00:17:55.532
Hey, Sachi! What's up?

00:17:55.616 --> 00:17:57.284
Come on. Let's play again.

00:17:57.367 --> 00:17:59.036
All right. But I'm definitely winning.

00:18:01.038 --> 00:18:04.875
Aoi, I found a first-year
that might be fun for you to play with.

00:18:04.958 --> 00:18:07.544
Who? Not the "Den Destroyer."

00:18:07.628 --> 00:18:11.799
No. This one took Library Prep Room
Number Two from me earlier today.

00:18:12.633 --> 00:18:15.803
Apparently, her new gambling den
is open for business.

00:18:15.886 --> 00:18:18.055
Why don't you go over and check it out?

00:18:18.138 --> 00:18:19.223
You better watch out!

00:18:19.306 --> 00:18:21.767
I'm going in for a counter
and another special.

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:24.353
-Huh? What's up?
-Hey. Sorry, Runa.

00:18:24.436 --> 00:18:26.313
-I got something to do.
-What?

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:29.316
Fighting games aren't fun
when I play by myself.

00:18:29.399 --> 00:18:31.151
Want me to send Kaede over here?

00:18:31.235 --> 00:18:33.612
Man, Kaede Manyuda is no fun.

00:18:33.695 --> 00:18:36.323
You know he won't play games with me.

00:18:36.406 --> 00:18:38.408
I'll come back and play with you later.

00:18:39.409 --> 00:18:40.494
LIMITED DICE GAME

00:18:40.577 --> 00:18:43.080
How long did Saotome say
it was gonna take?

00:18:43.163 --> 00:18:45.249
Probably another hour?

00:18:45.332 --> 00:18:47.167
It was stuff to finish her transfer.

00:18:47.251 --> 00:18:49.586
All righty.
So what do you think? Should we open?

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:50.963
I think it's time!

00:18:51.046 --> 00:18:52.589
You're excited about this.

00:18:53.173 --> 00:18:55.384
Yeah. Mary's helped me a lot.

00:18:55.467 --> 00:18:58.595
I wanna be able to start paying her back
for all she's done.

00:18:59.847 --> 00:19:01.598
[tense music playing]

00:19:01.682 --> 00:19:03.600
Hi! Come on in.

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:12.442
Sorry. That took longer than I thought.

00:19:12.526 --> 00:19:13.944
So what's going on here?

00:19:14.027 --> 00:19:15.904
Oh. Hey, Saotome.

00:19:15.988 --> 00:19:18.365
What's the matter? Are we losing already?

00:19:18.448 --> 00:19:20.242
No. We're up,

00:19:21.577 --> 00:19:22.995
by three million.

00:19:23.078 --> 00:19:24.997
Three million?

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:29.293
See him? That's Aoi Mibuomi
from the Student Council.

00:19:29.376 --> 00:19:31.003
He just kinda showed up

00:19:32.921 --> 00:19:34.256
I'll bet a million.

00:19:34.339 --> 00:19:35.174
Huh?

00:19:35.716 --> 00:19:37.593
Oh. That bet's a little too--

00:19:37.676 --> 00:19:39.136
What? Come on.

00:19:39.219 --> 00:19:42.097
You can afford to pay that amount
even if you do lose, right?

00:19:42.181 --> 00:19:44.600
You know, I bet I'll lose anyway.

00:19:44.683 --> 00:19:46.101
This game is hard to play.

00:19:46.185 --> 00:19:47.144
Huh?

00:19:47.769 --> 00:19:49.438
Okay. Let's play.

00:19:49.521 --> 00:19:51.732
You can play up to three rounds a day.

00:19:51.815 --> 00:19:53.984
Only three tries, huh?

00:19:54.776 --> 00:19:56.612
I wanna play with the white die.

00:19:57.404 --> 00:20:00.157
Okay, then.
I'll choose the red dice this round.

00:20:04.453 --> 00:20:05.495
[both gasping]

00:20:05.579 --> 00:20:08.373
Hurray, Hanatemari!
You rolled the high number!

00:20:08.457 --> 00:20:10.125
Now, the next round.

00:20:10.209 --> 00:20:11.376
Huh?

00:20:12.836 --> 00:20:14.379
Two million, please.

00:20:15.088 --> 00:20:17.591
Hanatemari won
the second match too.

00:20:17.674 --> 00:20:19.968
This next roll
will be the final one he's allowed to play

00:20:20.052 --> 00:20:21.887
before he hits the limit.

00:20:22.888 --> 00:20:24.139
Four million this time.

00:20:24.223 --> 00:20:25.641
Four million?

00:20:25.724 --> 00:20:27.392
-Huh?
-Hey, Mary.

00:20:27.476 --> 00:20:30.020
Oh! So, you're Mary Saotome!

00:20:30.604 --> 00:20:32.773
You know, I came all the way here for you.

00:20:32.856 --> 00:20:33.899
Huh?

00:20:33.982 --> 00:20:37.110
I heard you took out Juraku
in a game yesterday.

00:20:37.194 --> 00:20:38.654
That's pretty impressive.

00:20:40.948 --> 00:20:43.242
[Aoi] It looks like you put
a lot of thought into this game.

00:20:44.243 --> 00:20:47.746
It's clever that you have the customer
be the first one to pick out the die.

00:20:47.829 --> 00:20:49.331
They take the lead.

00:20:49.414 --> 00:20:52.167
Makes them feel
like the playing field is actually even.

00:20:52.251 --> 00:20:54.920
But, you and I both know that isn't true.

00:20:55.003 --> 00:20:56.922
It's a simple three-way deadlock.

00:20:57.965 --> 00:21:01.093
Red beats white,
white beats black, and black beats red.

00:21:01.176 --> 00:21:03.345
When they're pairs
it's a lot easier to win.

00:21:03.428 --> 00:21:04.429
But, with that said,

00:21:04.513 --> 00:21:06.765
whoever chooses later will win.

00:21:06.848 --> 00:21:09.184
-He's kidding.
-Is he serious?

00:21:09.268 --> 00:21:12.229
The probability says
there's a five-in-nine chance.

00:21:12.312 --> 00:21:15.190
The more times they get you to play,
the more the gambling den takes.

00:21:15.274 --> 00:21:17.276
It's a pretty sweet deal,

00:21:17.359 --> 00:21:19.736
taking advantage
of your customers like that.

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.446
<i>He's figured it out!</i>

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:22.948
The day is wasting.

00:21:23.031 --> 00:21:24.616
I could talk about this for hours,

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:27.202
but why don't we gamble
and test my theory.

00:21:27.786 --> 00:21:29.705
I'm gonna choose the white die again.

00:21:30.455 --> 00:21:31.957
You'll pick red, right?

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.458
Uh, y-yeah.

00:21:33.542 --> 00:21:35.711
<i>This is the "martingale" system! </i>

00:21:35.794 --> 00:21:38.964
<i>Every time he loses,</i>
<i>he'll double his previous bet!</i>

00:21:39.047 --> 00:21:41.216
<i>It doesn't matter how many times he loses,</i>

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:44.928
<i>he just needs to win once</i>
<i>to earn back everything he bet before.</i>

00:21:45.012 --> 00:21:48.849
<i>I've not come across this method</i>
<i>very often, mostly because of the risk.</i>

00:21:49.558 --> 00:21:51.852
<i>But if this guy came in here</i>
<i>to destroy us,</i>

00:21:51.935 --> 00:21:54.604
<i>this would be</i>
<i>the most effective way of doing it.</i>

00:21:54.688 --> 00:21:57.607
<i>Because if you somehow happen</i>
<i>to lose the first two rounds, </i>

00:21:57.691 --> 00:22:01.361
<i>your chances of winning the third</i>
<i>spike to 90%!</i>

00:22:02.904 --> 00:22:05.073
Hell yeah! Mibuomi wins!

00:22:05.157 --> 00:22:08.076
-Four million yen! That's amazing!
-Yeah!

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:09.911
<i>We only just started.</i>

00:22:09.995 --> 00:22:12.873
<i>I wasn't able to predict this</i>
<i>and figure out a plan.</i>

00:22:12.956 --> 00:22:14.333
<i>I'd already lost.</i>

00:22:17.169 --> 00:22:18.420
[Tsuzura groaning]

00:22:18.503 --> 00:22:20.339
Hanatemari!

00:22:20.422 --> 00:22:21.381
Are you okay?

00:22:21.465 --> 00:22:23.050
<i>Nothing will be left…</i>

00:22:23.133 --> 00:22:24.968
-Say something!
-I'm sorry.

00:22:31.933 --> 00:22:34.353
[Mary] Here's what we owe you.
One million yen.

00:22:35.937 --> 00:22:38.732
You can keep it. Let's call it a present.

00:22:38.815 --> 00:22:40.275
Huh?

00:22:40.359 --> 00:22:42.694
I figure you'll be in trouble
if you lose this,

00:22:42.778 --> 00:22:45.238
especially if you wanna reverse
her Mitten status.

00:22:45.322 --> 00:22:47.491
You're right, but I still don't--

00:22:47.574 --> 00:22:51.078
But if I do that, you think
you could help me with something?

00:22:52.079 --> 00:22:55.082
Mary, I really need you right now.

00:22:57.709 --> 00:22:59.669
It's not something that's difficult.

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:02.506
I just need your help with one thing.

00:23:06.093 --> 00:23:09.096
Destroying the Student Council President!

00:24:36.516 --> 00:24:41.021
Subtitle translation by: Helen O'Horan
